rsity’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers offers a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees, based on position, which includes: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits Life insurance coverage Employee discounts programs For detailed information on benefits and eligibility, please visit: http://uhr.rutgers.edu/benefits/benefits-overview . Posting Summary Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences – New Jersey Medical School Department of Pediatrics offers an opportunity for a Pediatric Hospitalist to join our faculty of more than 30 full-time clinicians and scientists at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. We are seeking physicians to provide patient care in the Division of Inpatient Pediatric Hospital Medicine and provide comprehensive evaluation and management for patients with other healthcare professionals to educate patients and their families about their conditions. In addition to patient care, the successful candidate will participate in the education of medical students and residents. The successful candidate will actively contribute to the primary missions of the Division of Inpatient Pediatric Hospital Medicine through accessible high quality health care, scholarly activity and education. Position Status Full Time Posting Number 26FA0839 Posting Open Date 09/28/2026 Posting Close Date 06/28/2027 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience MD degree Certifications/Licenses Board certified (or board-eligible) in Pediatrics and/or Pediatric Hospital Medicine. Candidate must possess (or eligible to apply for a valid NJ medical license, CDS and DEA . Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Applicant must demonstrate excellence as a clinician educator. Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview The Department of Pediatrics at Rutgers New Jersey Medical School is dedicated to the care of infants, children, adolescents and young adults. We are dedicated to managing and advancing the quality of life for our patients through excellence in care, education of future healthcare professionals, innovative research, and collaborative community outreach and partnership. Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants In addition to formally applying here, interested candidates must also submit a cover letter, three letters of reference, a current CV and complete contact information to: Marilyn Smith at smithma1@njms.rutgers.edu. For additional information, please contact Dr. Onajovwe Fofah, Professor and Chair, Department of Pediatrics at fofahon@njms.rutgers.edu or 973-972-5276 Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/281541 Campus Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences (RBHS) Home Location Campus Newark (RBHS) City Newark State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employment will commence during Flu Season, Rutgers University may require certain prospective employees to provide proof that they are vaccinated against Seasonal Influenza for the current Flu Season, unless the University has granted the individual a medical or religious exemption. Additional infection control and safety policies may apply. Prospective employees should speak with their hiring manager to determine which policies apply to the role or position for which they are applying. Failure to provide proof of vaccination for any required vaccines or obtain a medical or religious exemption from the University will result in rescission