    "https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/281853": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Maternal Fetal Medicine (L&amp;D Director)",
      "description": "Rutgers University Employment Opportunities | Open Rank - Maternal Fetal Medicine (L&amp;D Director) Skip to Main Content Universitywide | New Brunswick | Newark | Camden | RBHS University Search University Human Resources Home Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Why Work at Rutgers? Rutgers Edge The RU Commitment Benefits Information Information for New Employees URA-AFT Job Postings Rutgers University Foundation Job Postings Open Rank - Maternal Fetal Medicine (L&D Director) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Recruitment/Posting Title Open Rank - Maternal Fetal Medicine (L&D Director) Department RWJ - OB/GYN MFM/Atu Spmc Salary Details A minimum of $249,679 (Instructor); $388,180 (Asst Prof) OR $458,921 (Assoc. Prof) Offer Information The final salary offer may be determined by several factors, including, but not limited to, the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and expertise, and availability of department or grant funds to support the position. We also take into consideration market benchmarks, if and when appropriate, and internal equity to ensure fair compensation relative to the university’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers provides a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. The specific benefits vary based on the position and may include: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School seeks a Maternal-Fetal Medicine physician to serve as Medical Director of Labor and Delivery for Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital – New Brunswick and join the Division of Maternal-Fetal Medicine within the Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology, and Reproductive Sciences. The Medical Director will provide clinical and operational leadership for Labor and Delivery services, partnering with nursing, hospital, and physician leadership to ensure excellence in patient care, quality, safety, and operational performance. The successful candidate will also maintain an active Maternal-Fetal Medicine practice, caring for high-risk obstetric patients while contributing to the Division’s educational, research, and quality improvement missions. This is an open-rank faculty appointment with rank commensurate with experience and qualifications. Position Status Full Time Posting Number 26FA0814 Posting Open Date Posting Close Date 06/27/2027 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Medical degree (MD, DO, or equivalent). Residency in Obstetrics and Gynecology Fellowship in Maternal Medicine Skills: Excellent communication skills and a proven track record in multidisciplinary team collaboration. Certifications/Licenses Board certified or board eligible in Obstetrics and Gynecology, with subspecialty certification in Maternal–Fetal Medicine from the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology ( ABOG ). Eligible for medical licensure in the state of New Jersey. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Strongly Preferred Experience: Minimum of 3 years of clinical experience in a high acuity Labor and Delivery unit at an academic medical center These may influence the academic rank at which the candidate is appointed. Demonstrated commitment to teaching, mentorship, and supporting learners. Interest or experience in clinical research and scholarly activity. Experience working in an academic medical center. Prior involvement in quality‑improvement initiatives. A record of research publications and success in obtaining grant funding. Leadership experience in clinical care, education, or research. Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Standing, sitting, walking, talking or hearing. No special vision requirements. Overview Labor and Delivery Leadership, Clinical Operations, Patient Care: Serve as Medical Director of Labor and Delivery, providing clinical and operational leadership in partnership with nursing and hospital leadership. Oversee Labor and Delivery operations, including patient flow, triage efficiency, bed utilization, quality, safety, and patient experience. Lead multidisciplinary quality and safety initiatives, including safety huddles, peer review activities, root-cause analyses, and performance improvement efforts. Establish, implement, and promote adherence to evidence-based clinical protocols and best practices, including obstetric hemorrhage, hypertension, and fetal monitoring guidelines. Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams to ensure coordinated, high-quality care for low-risk and high-risk obstetric patients. Provide high-quality, evidence-based maternal-fetal medicine care, including outpatient and inpatient consultations, prenatal diagnosis, ultrasound, ultrasound-guided procedures, deliveries, and call coverage. Support growth of the maternal-fetal medicine program through clinical program development, outreach, and collaborative care initiatives. Education & Training: Teach and mentor maternal-fetal medicine fellows, residents, medical students, advanced practice providers, and other learners. Support the educational mission of the division and fellowship program through clinical teaching, conferences, lectures, and hands-on training. Foster a culture of professionalism, teamwork, and continuous learning. Research & Scholarly Activity: Participate in clinical, translational, and/or outcomes-based research and scholarly activities. Collaborate on research, quality improvement, and patient outcomes initiatives within the division, department, and health system. Support trainee scholarly activity, including presentations and publications. Other Administrative & Leadership Responsibilities: Partner with departmental, hospital, and nursing leadership to advance strategic, operational, and clinical priorities. Participate in departmental, institutional, and professional service activities, including committees, accreditation efforts, and program development. Promote a culture of collaboration, accountability, respect, and continuous improvement. Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/281067 Campus Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences (RBHS) Home Location Campus Downtown New Brunswick City New Brunswick State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employment will commence during Flu Season, Rutgers University may require certain prospective employees to provide proof that they are vaccinated against Seasonal Influenza for the current Flu Season, unless the University has granted the individual a medical or religious exemption. Additional infection control and safety policies may apply. Prospective employees should speak with their hiring manager to determine which policies apply to the role or position for which they are applying. Failure to provide proof of vaccination for any required vaccines or obtain a medical or religious exemption from the University will result in rescission of a candidate’s offer of employment or disciplinary action up to and including termination. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: http://uhr.rutgers.edu/non-discrimination-statement Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of Professional References (contact Info) Optional Documents It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: Non-Discrimination-Statement . In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and the New Jersey Law Against Discrimination (NJLAD), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation with regard to your access to and/or your participation in the application and selection processes (for example, the online application process or interviews), please call 848-932-3973 or e-mail us . Rutgers University is an equal access/equal opportunity institution. If you have trouble accessing this page because of a disability, please contact us at 732.745.7378 or via email at OneSource@Rutgers.edu . Rutgers University participates in the E-Verify program as required by law. Learn more about the E-Verify program . For technical assistance with the applicant tracking system (login, filling out your application, resetting your password, etc.) please contact the ROCS Help Desk at 848-932-4444 or ROCS@hr.rutgers.edu . To learn more about Rutgers University’s commitment to diversity and inclusion on its campuses, click here . Copyright © 2014 , Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution. Contact RU-info at 732-445-info (4639) | Questions? Ask Colonel Henry or text us at 732-662-2664. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
