    "https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/281511": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor / Nocturnist",
      "description": "Rutgers University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor / Nocturnist Skip to Main Content Universitywide | New Brunswick | Newark | Camden | RBHS University Search University Human Resources Home Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Why Work at Rutgers? Rutgers Edge The RU Commitment Benefits Information Information for New Employees URA-AFT Job Postings Rutgers University Foundation Job Postings Assistant Professor / Nocturnist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please upload CV. Position Details Position Information Recruitment/Posting Title Assistant Professor / Nocturnist Department RWJ - Emergency Medicine Salary Details Minimum of $379,000 Offer Information The final salary offer may be determined by several factors, including, but not limited to, the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and expertise, and availability of department or grant funds to support the position. We also take into consideration market benchmarks, if and when appropriate, and internal equity to ensure fair compensation relative to the university’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers provides a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. The specific benefits vary based on the position and may include: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary The Department of Emergency Medicine at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School a in New Brunswick, New Jersey, is seeking a board-certified or board-eligible Emergency Medicine physician to join our faculty as a Nocturnist . The Emergency Department manages more than 80,000 patient visits annually and serves as a regional referral center for trauma, critical care, stroke, cardiac emergencies, and complex tertiary care. The successful candidate will provide high-quality emergency care during overnight shifts while contributing to the department’s mission of excellence in patient care, education, and academic development. Faculty members work collaboratively with emergency medicine residents, medical students, advanced practice providers (APPs), nursing staff, and multidisciplinary consultants in a fast-paced academic environment. Position Status Full Time Posting Number 26FA0734 Posting Open Date 08/25/2026 Posting Close Date 07/13/2027 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Completed ACGME , Medical Residency Program, MD, DO Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Primary Responsibilities Clinical Care Provide comprehensive emergency medical care during designated overnight shifts. Evaluate, diagnose, and treat patients presenting with a broad spectrum of acute illnesses and injuries. Manage critically ill and injured patients in collaboration with trauma, surgical, medical, and specialty teams. Participate in departmental quality, safety, and patient experience initiatives. Maintain timely and accurate clinical documentation in the electronic medical record. Education and Supervision Supervise and provide clinical oversight for Emergency Medicine residents, off-service residents, medical students, and advanced practice providers. Foster a supportive learning environment that promotes clinical excellence and professional development. Deliver bedside teaching and procedural instruction during clinical shifts. Participate in resident and student evaluations and provide constructive feedback. Contribute to the department’s educational mission through lectures, conferences, simulation activities, and other didactic teaching opportunities as appropriate. Academic and Departmental Contributions Participate in departmental meetings, committees, and quality improvement initiatives. Engage in scholarly activity, research, educational innovation, or administrative projects consistent with faculty interests and departmental needs. Support ongoing accreditation, performance improvement, and patient safety efforts. Preferred Qualifications Qualifications MD or DO degree from an accredited medical school. Completion of an ACGME -accredited Emergency Medicine residency. Board-certified or board-eligible in Emergency Medicine. Eligible for unrestricted medical licensure in the State of New Jersey. DEA registration and appropriate hospital credentialing. Preferred Prior experience in academic emergency medicine. Demonstrated commitment to resident and medical student education. Interest in quality improvement, research, simulation, ultrasound, administration, or other academic pursuits. Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Please upload CV. Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279921 Campus Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences (RBHS) Home Location Campus Rutgers University - New Brunswick City New Brunswick State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employment will commence during Flu Season, Rutgers University may require certain prospective employees to provide proof that they are vaccinated against Seasonal Influenza for the current Flu Season, unless the University has granted the individual a medical or religious exemption. Additional infection control and safety policies may apply. Prospective employees should speak with their hiring manager to determine which policies apply to the role or position for which they are applying. Failure to provide proof of vaccination for any required vaccines or obtain a medical or religious exemption from the University will result in rescission of a candidate’s offer of employment or disciplinary action up to and including termination. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: http://uhr.rutgers.edu/non-discrimination-statement Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Optional Documents It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or