    "https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280446": {
      "title": "RBHS Faculty Instructor",
      "description": "Rutgers University Employment Opportunities | RBHS Faculty Instructor Skip to Main Content Universitywide | New Brunswick | Newark | Camden | RBHS University Search University Human Resources Home Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Why Work at Rutgers? Rutgers Edge The RU Commitment Benefits Information Information for New Employees URA-AFT Job Postings Rutgers University Foundation Job Postings RBHS Faculty Instructor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Recruitment/Posting Title RBHS Faculty Instructor Department RWJ - Psychiatry Research Salary Details $94,832 Offer Information The final salary offer may be determined by several factors, including, but not limited to, the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and expertise, and availability of department or grant funds to support the position. We also take into consideration market benchmarks, if and when appropriate, and internal equity to ensure fair compensation relative to the university’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers provides a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. The specific benefits vary based on the position and may include: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary The Department of Psychiatry at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School ( RWJMS ) seeks a Faculty Instructor to expand our research portfolio in network and computational neuroscience approaches to psychiatric illness. The Instructor will be housed within the laboratory of Dr. Avram Holmes and will work to support the research initiatives of that group/lab under the supervision of the lab head. Priority will be given to work aligned with the Center for Advanced Human Brain Imaging Research ( CAHBIR ; ( https://sites.rutgers.edu/cahbir/ ). We seek candidates with expertise in network neuroscience, computational modeling, neuroimaging, and related approaches to understanding psychiatric illness. The Faculty Instructor will conduct collaborative research, contribute to the department’s strategic research initiatives, and work closely with a multidisciplinary team. The position includes faculty mentorship and is intended as a transitional appointment to a faculty career track. Appointment is contingent on funding and is limited to a maximum of three years. Position Status Full Time Posting Number 26FA0745 Posting Open Date Posting Close Date Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES include the following. Other duties may be assigned. 1. Performs research activities related to neuroimaging and psychopathology as directed by their faculty supervisor/principal investigator (PI). 2. Leads the design and implementation of research projects, from study conceptualization, through collection, and analyses under the supervision of the PI. 3. In consultation with the PI, plan, design, and contribute to the submission of large-scale federal grant applications. 4. Publishes results in peer-reviewed journals, presents at national and international conferences, and presents within their home and peer institutions. In consultation with the PI, assist in the coordination and organization of departmental/center/program linked talk series. 5. If supported and/or directed by the faculty supervisor, submit application(s) as a principal investigator for extramural funding to conduct novel research within the scope of the research group’s/lab’s research interests, and which includes salary support for the incumbent’s (faculty Instructor) position. 6. Assists with research compliance activities, including communications with funders (i.e. NIH ), maintaining up-to-date research training and certifications, IRB or IACUC applications, and other activities. 7. Manages communication with external collaborators. 8. Documents research activities, maintains a database of up-to-date research protocols, and manages and organizes large datasets that have been generated in the service of research projects. 9. Supervises undergraduates, technicians, graduate students and post-doctoral fellows. 10. Performs other related duties as required. Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280325 Campus Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences (RBHS) Home Location Campus Piscataway (RBHS) City Piscataway State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employment will commence during Flu Season, Rutgers University may require certain prospective employees to provide proof that they are vaccinated against Seasonal Influenza for the current Flu Season, unless the University has granted the individual a medical or religious exemption. Additional infection control and