    "https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277677": {
      "title": "Physician Faculty (Instructor/Assistant Professor/Associate Professor) for Complex and Minimally Invasive Gynecological Surgery",
      "description": "Rutgers University Employment Opportunities | Physician Faculty (Instructor/Assistant Professor/Associate Professor) for Complex and Minimally Invasive Gynecological Surgery Skip to Main Content Universitywide | New Brunswick | Newark | Camden | RBHS University Search University Human Resources Home Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Why Work at Rutgers? Rutgers Edge The RU Commitment Benefits Information Information for New Employees URA-AFT Job Postings Rutgers University Foundation Job Postings Physician Faculty (Instructor/Assistant Professor/Associate Professor) for Complex and Minimally Invasive Gynecological Surgery Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Recruitment/Posting Title Physician Faculty (Instructor/Assistant Professor/Associate Professor) for Complex and Minimally Invasive Gynecological Surgery Department RWJ - Obstetrics & Gynocology Salary Details A minimum of $243,137 (Instructor); $319,523 (Asst Prof) OR $374,412 (Assoc. Prof) Offer Information The final salary offer may be determined by several factors, including, but not limited to, the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and expertise, and availability of department or grant funds to support the position. We also take into consideration market benchmarks, if and when appropriate, and internal equity to ensure fair compensation relative to the university’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers provides a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. The specific benefits vary based on the position and may include: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary The Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology and Reproductive Sciences at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School is seeking a fellowship-trained, board-eligible or board-certified Complex Benign and Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgeon to join the newly established Division of Complex and Minimally Invasive Gynecological Surgery ( CMIGS ). This is a full-time, open-rank academic position in an innovative and growing program that serves as a regional referral center for complex benign gynecologic conditions. About the Division of Complex and Minimally Invasive Gynecological Surgery. The Division provides comprehensive surgical care for patients with complex gynecologic conditions including, but not limited to, endometriosis, large-volume fibroids, pelvic pain, adhesions, isthmoceles, C-section scar ectopic pregnancies, adnexal pathology, abnormal uterine bleeding, and congenital anomalies. The Division emphasizes minimally invasive laparoscopic, robotic, hysteroscopic, and/or vaginal surgical techniques and is committed to advancing the field through research, education, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Key Responsibilities Provide advanced minimally invasive, laparoscopic, robotic, hysteroscopic, and/or vaginal surgical care for complex benign gynecologic conditions. Participate in the education of medical students and OB/ GYN residents through clinical teaching and simulation training. Collaborate on quality improvement initiatives within gynecologic surgery. Engage in clinical or translational research aligned with Division priorities. Support the development of a formal referral program and interdisciplinary partnerships. Position Status Full Time Posting Number 26FA0630 Posting Open Date 06/23/2026 Posting Close Date Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience MD/DO degree or equivalent with board eligibility or certification in Obstetrics and Gynecology. Completion of a fellowship in Complex Benign/Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery or equivalent. Certifications/Licenses Eligible for medical licensure, DEA and CDS in the state of New Jersey. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Preferred fellowship is AAGL -accredited Demonstrated excellence in clinical care, teaching, and scholarship. Strong interpersonal and communication skills with a commitment to interdisciplinary care. Enthusiasm for patient care, medical student and resident education. Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Standing, sitting, walking, talking or hearing. No special vision requirements. Overview Clinical Care Provide direct surgical and outpatient care in advanced benign gynecology, including but not limited to the management of: Endometriosis and chronic pelvic pain Uterine fibroids Mullerian anomalies Isthmoceles and abnormal (ie. C-section scar) ectopic pregnancies Intrauterine adhesions Large uteri hysterectomy Other complex benign gynecologic surgery Perform minimally invasive surgery using laparoscopic, robotic, hysteroscopic, and vaginal techniques. Participate in multidisciplinary care and expand access to tertiary-level gynecologic surgical services. Help develop standardized clinical pathways, referral guidelines, and preoperative protocols. Complete all required clinical documentation, reports, claims, and correspondence in a timely and accurate manner. Maintain timely contracting and credentialing with public and private payors. Devote the necessary time, attention, and professional effort to deliver care consistent with accepted community standards of practice. Teaching & Education Teach and mentor medical students and residents in gynecology and surgical technique. Serve as a faculty leader in surgical simulation and skills development. Participate in curriculum development for gynecologic surgery at all levels of training. Support departmental efforts to grow a future AAGL -accredited Complex Benign/ MIGS fellowship Provide lectures, participate in Grand Rounds, mentor trainees, and contribute to the educational mission of the department. Provide education and training for APNs, nurses, sonographers, and other third?party contractor personnel as needed. Academic / Scholarly Activity Engage in scholarly activity with a focus on clinical outcomes, surgical innovation, health disparities, or pelvic pain. Collaborate with faculty across disciplines to support grant submissions, publications, and research mentorship. Present work at regional and national academic meetings. Maintain and enhance professional competency, including board certification and state licensure, and engage in ongoing professional development. Administrative / Departmental Service Participate in departmental meetings, hospital committees, and institutional initiatives. Collaborate with faculty across disciplines to support grant submissions, publications, and research mentorship. Present work at regional and national academic meetings. Collaborate with departmental leadership and colleagues to advance the mission of the medical school and health system. Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277217 Campus Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences (RBHS) Home Location Campus Downtown New Brunswick City New Brunswick State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employment will commence during Flu Season, Rutgers University may require certain prospective employees to provide proof that they are vaccinated against Seasonal Influenza for the current Flu Season, unless the University has granted the individual a medical or religious exemption. Additional infection control and safety policies may apply. Prospective employees should speak with their hiring manager to determine which policies apply to the role or position for which they are applying. Failure to provide proof of vaccination for any required vaccines or obtain a medical or religious exemption from the University will result in rescission of a candidate’s offer of employment or disciplinary action up to and including termination. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: http://uhr.rutgers.edu/non-discrimination-statement Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of Professional References (contact Info) It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: Non-Discrimination-Statement . In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and the New Jersey Law Against Discrimination (NJLAD), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation with regard to your access to and/or your participation in the application and selection processes (for example, the online application process or interviews), please call 848-932-3973 or e-mail us . Rutgers University is an equal access/equal opportunity institution. If you have trouble accessing this page because of a disability, please contact us at 732.745.7378 or via email at OneSource@Rutgers.edu . Rutgers University participates in the E-Verify program as required by law. Learn more about the E-Verify program . For technical assistance with the applicant tracking system (login, filling out your application, resetting your password, etc.) please contact the ROCS Help Desk at 848-932-4444 or ROCS@hr.rutgers.edu . To learn more about Rutgers University’s commitment to diversity and inclusion on its campuses, click here . Copyright © 2014 , Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution. Contact RU-info at 732-445-info (4639) | Questions? Ask Colonel Henry or text us at 732-662-2664. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
