    "https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268720": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor/Ambulatory Care/Psych",
      "description": "Rutgers University Employment Opportunities | Clinical Assistant Professor/Ambulatory Care/Psych Skip to Main Content Universitywide | New Brunswick | Newark | Camden | RBHS University Search University Human Resources Home Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Why Work at Rutgers? Rutgers Edge The RU Commitment Benefits Information Information for New Employees URA-AFT Job Postings Rutgers University Foundation Job Postings Clinical Assistant Professor/Ambulatory Care/Psych Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Recruitment/Posting Title Clinical Assistant Professor/Ambulatory Care/Psych Department Pharmacy Practice & Administra Salary Details 115,000 Offer Information The final salary offer may be determined by several factors, including, but not limited to, the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and expertise, and availability of department or grant funds to support the position. We also take into consideration market benchmarks, if and when appropriate, and internal equity to ensure fair compensation relative to the university’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers provides a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. The specific benefits vary based on the position and may include: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary The Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy at Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track faculty position. The faculty member will hold a clinical appointment in Inpatient Behavioral Health at Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital Somerset. The pharmacy school is recognized at all levels—local, state, national, and international—as offering one of the most challenging, dynamic, and rewarding programs leading to the Doctor of Pharmacy degree. Alongside supportive faculty and staff, students at the school develop a foundation for learning that lasts well beyond graduation. The Department of Pharmacy Practice and Administration emphasizes the clinical and regulatory aspects of pharmacy practice. Its mission is to prepare students to deliver pharmaceutical care in various practice settings. Graduates are equipped with the skills needed to adapt to a constantly evolving healthcare environment. Students also gain a solid foundation in scientific principles, ethics, and attitudes necessary for lifelong adaptation to changes in healthcare. This mission supports the overall goals of the Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy in four key areas: teaching, practice, scholarship, and service. Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital Somerset ( RWJUH Somerset) is a 343-bed community hospital in Somerville, NJ, serving as a teaching site for Rutgers University and hosting the Somerset Family Medicine Residency Program. It has earned national recognition for clinical quality and safety, including the Magnet® Award for Nursing Excellence and an “A” Hospital Safety Grade from Leapfrog. In 2025, it was named one of America’s 250 Best Hospitals by Healthgrades, ranking in the top 5% nationally. RWJUH Somerset was also recognized as a “Leader in LGBT Health Care Equality” by the Human Rights Campaign, becoming the first NJ hospital to provide primary care for the LGBTQIA+ community. The hospital remains committed to delivering high-quality care, continuously adopting the latest evidence and technology. This inpatient psychiatry unit (5W) has 27 beds and serves both voluntary and involuntary psychiatric patients. Care includes daily multidisciplinary rounds for every patient and daily therapeutic group sessions. Once stabilized, patients are transferred from 5W to the onsite partial hospitalization program and clinic for ongoing care. Additionally, the outpatient eating disorder unit has 20 beds, with daily psychiatry rounds and group sessions. While the position focuses on inpatient care, there is room for growth to support other psychiatry services. The Behavioral Health clinical pharmacist faculty member will collaborate with pharmacists, nurses, and medical staff to optimize patient care in our Behavioral Health program across inpatient, emergency department, and ambulatory (outpatient offices/clinics) settings, with a primary focus on inpatient care. The faculty member will organize, develop, and participate in clinical and quality improvement activities. Clinical activities include, but are not limited to the following: practice under collaborative practice agreement to optimize inpatient and outpatient pharmacotherapy, participation in quality initiatives to reduce readmissions, enhance medication access, participation in multidisciplinary rounds, provide interprofessional education, collaboration on policy and procedure development, committee participation, perform research and medication use evaluations, conduct dosing consults, support Medication Assistance Treatment initiatives, provide community outreach support, and precept Advanced Pharmacy Practice Experiential students and Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital Somerset Post-graduate year 1 pharmacy practice residents on their psychiatry rotation. Applicants must have a Doctor of Pharmacy degree and have completed at least two years of residency training with a PGY -2 in psychiatry/Behavioral Health or equivalent experience. Candidates must be highly motivated, innovative, and team-oriented and possess excellent communication and interpersonal skills to provide patient-centered care with a commitment to teaching, service, and professional advancement. Board certification is preferred. Eligibility for licensure as a pharmacist in the State of New Jersey is required. Position Status Full Time Posting Number 26FA0114 Posting Open Date 02/09/2026 Posting Close Date Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Applicants must have a Doctor of Pharmacy degree and have completed at least two years of residency training with a PGY -2 in Psychiatry/Behavioral Health or equivalent experience. Certifications/Licenses Board certification is preferred. Eligibility for licensure as a pharmacist in the State of New Jersey is required. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Candidates must be highly motivated, innovative, and team-oriented and possess excellent communication skills to provide patient-centered care with a commitment to teaching, service, and professional advancement. Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268385 Campus Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences (RBHS) Home Location Campus Rutgers University - New Brunswick City Piscataway State NJ Location Details Split time between Rutgers Busch Campus and Site Location, Robert Wood Johnson Hospital, Somerset, NJ. Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employment will commence during Flu Season, Rutgers University may require certain prospective employees to provide proof that they are vaccinated against Seasonal Influenza for the current Flu Season, unless the University has granted the individual a medical or religious exemption. Additional infection control and safety policies may apply. Prospective employees should speak with their hiring manager to determine which policies apply to the role or position for which they are applying. Failure to provide proof of vaccination for any required vaccines or obtain a medical or religious exemption from the University will result in rescission of a candidate’s offer of employment or disciplinary action up to and including termination. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: http://uhr.rutgers.edu/non-discrimination-statement Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae List of Professional References (contact Info) Certifications/Licenses Optional Documents It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, na