d savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary The Department of Restorative Dentistry at Rutgers School of Dental Medicine is seeking general dentists for a non-tenure track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The successful candidate will have a .50 FTE commitment to teaching. Specific responsibilities include participation in both didactic and clinical teaching of Restorative Dentistry (Operative Dentistry, Fixed Prosthodontics, and Removable Prosthodontics) to our pre-doctoral dental students, as well as participation in other predoctoral educational programs of the Department. The successful candidate will possess strong leadership and teamwork skills. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interviews of qualified candidates will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: · Clinical Teaching · Preclinical Laboratory Teaching · Seminars · Lectures · Other duties as assigned by Chair Position Status Part Time Posting Number 23FA0002 Posting Open Date 01/06/2023 Posting Close Date Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Candidates must possess a DDS / DMD or an equivalent dental degree. Previous academic teaching and proven research experience are preferred; Strong leadership and teamwork skills. Certifications/Licenses Candidates must possess a DDS / DMD or an equivalent dental degree; · Currently hold or be eligible for dental licensure in the State of New Jersey; Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Physical requirements for this position include regularly walking, reaching with hands and arms, occasionally stooping, bending and lifting. Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/po